// variant with a fixed target kind and availability under every gate applicable
// to that verb. Every compiled Attack, turn-clock Move, and End Turn has a
// non-empty selector. Every compiled Attack carries its exact full-ref
// AttackRef and every current live-sight member except the actor exactly once,
// including unavailable candidates and their target-specific reasons; a live
// holding with no position fails Afford. Candidate why is present if and only
// if candidate available is false. Candidate-level TARGET_OUT_OF_REACH remains
// alongside its row; declaration-level NO_TARGET_IN_REACH disables the Attack
// without removing rows.
//
// EARLY BLOCKERS ARE ROWS, NOT OMISSIONS. If a per-verb gate stops compilation,
// Afford still emits that verb's declaration (including Attack) with
// available=false, why present, empty id, absent attack, empty candidates, and
// its fixed target kind. Compiled offers disabled by later budget/target gates
// retain their non-empty id and, for Attack, attack and candidate rows. The
// fixed mapping for compiled and blocked rows is Attack -> MEMBER, Move -> PATH,
