//   - MASKED AS WALL IN GEOMETRY, IN ONE CASE ONLY: for a concealed
//     door between two spaces the member can see, `boundaries` gains a
//     synthetic ordinary boundary at the door's edges, indistinguishable
//     from an authored wall — nothing marks it. Masked rather than
//     omitted because a door's edges carry no authored boundary (a door
