//     does not hide unexplored space, so the map itself must keep the
//     secret). A non-knower's answer is BYTE-IDENTICAL to an atlas in
//     which the concealed region was never authored: its cells withheld
//     from `cells`, its AtlasRegion from `regions`, its props from
//     `props`, and EVERY boundary touching its cells from `boundaries` —
//     border walls included. Withholding only interior boundaries was
//     the leak the refinement closed: a border wall left behind would
//     touch no visible floor, an impossible signature in an honest
//     atlas, certifying hidden space at a named coordinate. With the
//     whole border withheld, the space reads as solid mass exactly like
//     anywhere beyond the map's edge — and no mask applies at the
//     region's border: its door's edge already reads as solid mass like
//     the rest of it, and a synthetic wall touching void would carry the
//     same self-marking signature. Every entrance of a concealed region
//     is itself a concealed door (authoring refuses anything else), each
//     absent from the door-lists per the first half; the mask stays the
//     second half's own.
//
