// SearchResponse acknowledges that the search happened, and deliberately
// nothing more.
//
// THE ANSWER NEVER LEAKS THE QUESTION. An empty room and a failed check
// answer with these same bytes — a response that said anything about
// outcome would tell a failed searcher whether there had been something to
// find, which is the one thing a failed search must not learn. So there is
// no found list, no roll, no count, and no seq: nothing here varies with
// what the room holds. A find reaches the searcher the way all world
// change reaches anybody — as a beat (design rule 2): DOOR_REVEALED on
// their own stream, audience = the searcher alone.
//
// saved and delivery are S6's law, kept by every mutating verb at this
